4.9 Life Members and Honorary Members shall not be required to pay any subscription, fee, or charge, save for such usage charges as may be levied under clause 4.4. This exemption does not extend to the monthly fee for Club Social Membership, which shall be payable by any Life Member or Honorary Member who also holds Social Membership.

**5. GENERAL MEETINGS**

5.1 The Annual General Meeting of the Club shall be held in March of each year, on a date to be fixed by the Committee. The Secretary shall give at least 21 days’ written notice of the meeting to all members, specifying the business to be transacted.

5.2 The business of the Annual General Meeting shall include:
(a) the receipt of the Chair’s report on the affairs of the Club;
(b) the receipt of the Treasurer’s report and the audited accounts for the previous membership year;
(c) the election of the Committee and officers;
(d) the appointment of an auditor or independent examiner;
(e) the ratification of any changes to subscriptions and fees;
(f) any other business of which due notice has been given.

5.3 An Extraordinary General Meeting may be called at any time by the Committee, or upon the written requisition of not fewer than twenty members. The requisition shall state the purpose of the meeting, and no other business shall be transacted at that meeting.

5.4 Fourteen days’ written notice shall be given for an Extraordinary General Meeting, specifying the business to be transacted. The meeting shall be held within 28 days of the date on which the requisition is received by the Secretary.

5.5 The quorum for a General Meeting shall be twenty members, or one-tenth of the total membership, whichever is the lesser. If a quorum is not present within thirty minutes of the time appointed for the meeting, the meeting shall stand adjourned to the same day in the following week at the same time and place, or to such other time and place as the Committee may determine. At the adjourned meeting, the members present shall constitute a quorum.

5.6 Each member present at a General Meeting shall have one vote on any motion put to the meeting. Voting shall be by a show of hands unless a secret ballot is demanded by not fewer than five members. In the case of an equality of votes, the Chair shall have a casting vote.

