5.7 The Chair of the meeting shall conduct the proceedings in an orderly manner and shall have the power to adjourn the meeting for a period not exceeding thirty minutes, or for such longer period as the meeting may decide.

5.8 Minutes of every General Meeting shall be kept by the Secretary and shall be confirmed at the next General Meeting, signed by the Chair, and retained in the Club’s minute book. Any member may inspect the minutes at a reasonable time upon application to the Secretary.

**6. THE COMMITTEE**

6.1 The affairs of the Club shall be managed by a Committee consisting of the following officers and members:
(a) the Chair;
(b) the Vice-Chair;
(c) the Secretary;
(d) the Treasurer;
(e) the Membership Secretary;
(f) the Facilities Manager;
(g) not fewer than three and not more than six ordinary members.

6.2 The Committee shall be elected at the Annual General Meeting and shall hold office from the conclusion of that meeting until the conclusion of the next Annual General Meeting. All members of the Committee shall be Full Members of the Club, save that the Membership Secretary may be a Social Member.

6.3 Casual vacancies on the Committee may be filled by co-option. A person co-opted to fill a vacancy shall hold office until the next Annual General Meeting and shall have full voting rights.

6.4 The Committee shall meet not fewer than six times in each membership year. The Secretary shall give at least seven days’ written notice of each meeting, together with the agenda and minutes of the previous meeting.
